    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 265277,
        "name": "",
        "username": "Nightsider",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/b5e925/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-03-27T18:15:38.531Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey everyone!</p>\n<p>I found the old Google Sheet character builder made by Justin Wawrzonek AKA drevilz4l AKA Beeromancer Macduff, and I gave it a massive upgrade!</p>\n<p>He encouraged me to share it here. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>It has a campaign (collection) planner, with Hero character builder and output sheet. Villain builder, collection planner, scene planner, notes sections, and rules quick ref (including some a house rule clarification regarding “remove penalty” type abilities).</p>\n<p>There’s a few formatting quirks and type-o’s I may have missed.</p>\n<p>Just like Beeromancer’s original, create a copy of the sheet and save it to your Google sheets, and edit as needed.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/10iL3chpFToog3AcTpfCs2ppDpG06AyicTQqX6x1_lDw/edit?usp=sharing\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">SCRPG Ultimate Collection Planner Template</a></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-03-27T18:15:38.531Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 8,
        "reads": 21,
        "readers_count": 20,
        "score": 119.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 32227,
        "topic_slug": "ulitmate-collection-planner",
        "display_username": "",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
